<title>USA: E-Z-EM unit gets FDA okay on liver set.</title>
<headline>E-Z-EM unit gets FDA okay on liver set.</headline>
<dateline>QUEENSBURY, N.Y. 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>AngioDynamics Inc, a subsidiary of E-Z-EM Inc, said Tuesday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has granted 510(k) clearance for the company to market its Transjugular Access Set.</p>
<p>The product is a series of coaxial catheters and needles that are designed to reach the liver though a small puncture in the jugular vein in the neck.</p>
<p>The company said that it estimates that the number of minimally invasive liver access procedures worldwide this year will be about 35,000 and that the total is growing.</p>
</text>
